package CanvasNet {
    part def HelpTopics {
        doc /* The catalog of help topics of the tool, shipped inside the tool as embedded resources so that it works offline and matches the installed version: ten topics in a fixed order (scad, vega-lite, svg, pdf, pptx, vsdx, raster, json, errors, and limits), each with a title, a summary, aliases (for example openscad, vl, powerpoint, visio, and png or jpg for raster), sections, and examples. A topic of an input format has the sections supported, unsupported, options, diagnostics (and how --strict treats them), and known differences, and at least two examples; the topics json, errors, and limits describe the result documents, the error codes and exit codes, and the size and resource limits. The numbers in the text are tokens resolved from the constants of the code when the topic loads. An example is either source text, shipped as a file next to the topic and verified to render with --strict without a diagnostic, or a command line. The unit finds a topic by name or alias ignoring case (names and aliases never collide with a command, help, or topics), and renders a topic, the list of its examples, and one example as plain text (no color codes, wrapped to 78 columns without splitting a word, deterministic) or as a JSON document (kinds topic, examples, and example); an unknown example name is a usage error listing the names. The content is verified against the code (the options of the render command, every error code, the cited diagnostic identifiers and what triggers them, and the limits) so that it cannot drift. It is used by the CommandRegistry unit, which owns the help command, and by the help examples self-test of the Validation unit. */

        comment sourceRef /* Source: src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Tool/Commands/HelpTopics.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Tool/Commands/HelpTopics.Render.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Tool/Commands/Help/ (the embedded topic files and the examples in Help/Examples/) */
        comment testRef /* Test: test/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Tool.Tests/Commands/HelpTopicsTests.cs, test/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Tool.Tests/Commands/HelpTopicsTests.Triggers.cs */
        comment designRef /* Design: docs/design/canvas-net-tool/commands/help-topics.md */
        comment verificationRef /* Verification: docs/verification/canvas-net-tool/commands/help-topics.md */
        comment reqRef /* Requirements: docs/reqstream/canvas-net-tool/commands/help-topics.yaml */
    }
}
